          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "The dominant reflections index to a rhombohedral CrF\u2083-type framework in \\(R\\bar 3c\\), with approximately \\(a=5.102\\) \u00c5 and \\(c=13.466\\) \u00c5. Representative indexing is 012 at 24.07\u00b0, 104 at 33.43\u00b0, 110 at 35.15\u00b0, 024 at 49.29\u00b0, 116 at 54.4\u00b0, and 208 at 70.2\u00b0.\n\nBecause O and F differ by only one electron, their ordering cannot be determined reliably from this Cu X-ray powder pattern. The CIF therefore gives the diffraction-supported average structure, with O/F disorder on the anion site. Several split components indicate a minor symmetry-lowered distortion or metric variant, but there is insufficient information to construct a unique ordered alternative.\n\n```cif\ndata_Cr4OF11_average\n_audit_creation_method                 'Indexed and modeled from Cu Kalpha1 powder diffraction'\n_chemical_name_common                  'chromium oxide fluoride, average CrF3-type structure'\n_chemical_formula_structural           'Cr4OF11'\n_chemical_formula_sum                  'Cr F2.75 O0.25'\n_chemical_formula_weight               108.2415\n_cell_formula_units_Z                  6\n\n_diffrn_radiation_type                 'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength           1.5406\n\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt              'R -3 c:H'\n_space_group_IT_number                 167\n_symmetry_cell_setting                 trigonal\n_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M         'R -3 c:H'\n\n_cell_length_a                         5.1021(20)\n_cell_length_b                         5.1021(20)\n_cell_length_c                         13.466(6)\n_cell_angle_alpha                      90\n_cell_angle_beta                       90\n_cell_angle_gamma                      120\n_cell_volume                           303.6(3)\n_exptl_crystal_density_diffrn          3.55\n\nloop_\n_atom_type_symbol\n_atom_type_oxidation_number\nCr  3.25\nF  -1\nO  -2\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_B_iso_or_equiv\nCr1  Cr   6  b  0.00000  0.00000  0.00000  1.000000  0.40\nF1   F   18  e  0.435(5) 0.00000  0.25000  0.916667  0.70\nO1   O   18  e  0.435(5) 0.00000  0.25000  0.083333  0.70\n```\n\nThe occupancies give, per hexagonal cell, Cr\\(_6\\)F\\(_{16.5}\\)O\\(_{1.5}\\), equivalent to Cr\\(_4\\)OF\\(_{11}\\). The anion coordinate is approximate; neutron diffraction, electron diffraction, or total-scattering data would be needed to resolve an ordered lower-symmetry model.",
